# EduFix AI — UI Screen Rules

Before implementing any screen or UI change, verify it against this checklist.

## Mobile First (mandatory)

- Design first for **390px–430px** viewport width.
- Then adapt to tablet and desktop. Never desktop-first.
- Primary users: students on phones. UI should feel like a modern mobile app (Linear / Vercel / Material 3).

```tsx
{/* ✅ Base styles = mobile; enhance with sm/md/lg */}
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 px-4 py-6 md:mx-auto md:max-w-3xl md:px-8">

{/* ❌ Desktop grid as default, then squeeze for mobile */}
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-8 max-md:grid-cols-1">
```

## Touch & Accessibility

- Interactive controls: minimum **44×44px** hit area (`min-h-11 min-w-11` or equivalent padding).
- High contrast (WCAG AA). Visible focus rings. Accessible labels / ARIA when needed.
- Prefer clarity over decoration: generous whitespace, soft radii, discreet shadows, elegant transitions.

## Components

- Build reusable pieces; colocate under `src/components/` (or feature folders).
- Prefer shadcn/ui primitives; do not duplicate one-off styled buttons/cards.

## Motion — GSAP only

- **Only** GSAP for animations. No Framer Motion, CSS infinite loops as primary UX motion, particles, animated backgrounds, or Three.js.
- Motion must **inform** (entrance, counters, cards, section reveal, AI flow, confirmations) — never distract.
- Prefer short durations (~200–300ms). No infinite decorative animations.
- Mark animatable nodes with `data-gsap="..."` for future hooks when wiring GSAP.

## Pre-ship checklist

1. Readable and usable at ~400px width without horizontal scroll.
2. Primary CTAs ≥ 44×44px.
3. No non-GSAP animation libraries introduced.
4. Layout starts mobile; larger breakpoints only enhance.
5. High contrast text/icons; decorative noise minimized.
